# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Secrets
*.pem
*.key
*.secret
.env*
kubeconfig*
*.kubeconfig
# Go sources like bootstrap/internal/talos/kubeconfig.go are code, not credentials
!kubeconfig*.go

# Bootstrap runtime state — plaintext working cache (regenerable).
# The encrypted vault/ under each cluster is committed; only the decrypted
# working copies are ignored.
clusters/*/secrets/
clusters/*/nodes/
clusters/*/state/
clusters/*/*.log
logs/

# Superpowers working docs (plans/specs are local scratch, not repo artifacts)
docs/superpowers/

# Terraform plan files embed resolved variable values, including ones sourced
# from the vaulted tfvars. They are also point-in-time — applying a stale plan
# diverges from real state — so they are never worth keeping. The extensionless
# spellings come first because `-out=tfplan` is what this repo's own docs tell
# you to run; terraform/.gitignore only catches those under terraform/.
tfplan
tfplan.*
tfdestroy-plan
*.tfplan

# etcd snapshots contain every Kubernetes Secret in plaintext, so this matches
# the whole extension rather than the naming conventions we happen to have used
# — `etcdctl snapshot save` defaults to a bare snapshot.db. No .db file has ever
# been tracked here, so there is nothing legitimate to exclude.
*.db

# Agent-created git worktrees live inside the checkout.
.claude/worktrees/
worktrees/
.worktrees/
